Jakob Creutzig  <creutzig@mathematik.tu-darmstadt.de> wrote:
>Gnus looks for the last "-- " and shows the text 
>below it as signature, ignoring any preceding "-- ".  
>To elaborate whether this is conforming to standards 
>is left as an exercise to the reader.  

I don't believe there is any formal standard here, as is so often the case
with Usenet. I would say that a message should not contain "\n-- \n"
except at the start of the signature (except for experimental purposes)
and hence the behaviour of newsreaders when faced with such a malformed
article might correctly be to treat either or neither as the separator.
